Random Walk Search Implementation
Overview

A Random Walk Search algorithm was added using both the Template Pattern and Strategy Pattern.

The algorithm randomly selects neighboring nodes during traversal until the destination is found.

Example Graph Search

Example search:

GraphSearch("a", "c", Algorithm.RANDOM)

The algorithm may generate different traversal outputs each time due to randomness.

Example Output
Run 1
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}]}
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}, Node{b}]}
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}, Node{b}, Node{c}]}
Run 2
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}]}
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}, Node{e}]}
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}, Node{e}, Node{g}]}
visiting Path{nodes=[Node{a}, Node{b}, Node{c}]}
Why Random Walk Was Added

The Random Walk algorithm demonstrates extensibility of the design patterns and supports randomized traversal behavior.

